 # AdrenoMetal
 
+The frontend library answers Core Image's `newExternFunctionWithName:` through
+the existing function lookup, including extern kernel functions and their retained
+library bitcode. A missing name remains nil. This matches the selector used by
+the iPhone24A446 precompiled-kernel path; complete icon rendering remains a hardware
+check.
+
+Single-sample tiled heap output with multiple levels uses the existing
+tile-coordinate conversion once per eligible level. Each dispatch has its own
+shape and descriptor set; staging bytes, image transfers, copy-back ranges and
+independent-writer merges retain their original behavior. CPU Vulkan tests cover
+two-level and twelve-level images, padding and fallback layouts.
+
 AdrenoMetal publishes a Metal device through `MTLAddDevice`. It translates AIR through metal2vulkan, compiles SPIR-V with Turnip, and submits work to [Adreno740](/drivers/adreno740). Firmware, power votes and display integration come from the board.
 
